{
  "baseRefName": "main",
  "body": "## Summary\n- add fail-closed unlocked-desktop Windows certification harness and self-hosted workflow\n- add ignored UIA/input/pointer/clipboard and WGC picker interactive tests\n- parse the PowerShell harness in hosted Windows CI without executing interactive claims\n- update Windows authority docs and release blockers to match merged native CI evidence\n\n## Claim discipline\nHosted Actions remain PASS_WINDOWS_NATIVE_CI only. The new workflow requires a self-hosted Windows runner labeled semwright-interactive. Unexecuted rows remain WINDOWS_INTERACTIVE_PENDING; external MCP filesystem mounts remain BLOCKED_PORTABLE_PATH_VIRTUALIZATION.\n\n## Local validation\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check\n- git diff --check\n- workflow YAML parse\n- release-readiness.json parse\n\nHeavy/native validation is delegated to GitHub Actions.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "IC_kwDOUkU25s8AAAABXauVpQ",
      "author": {
        "login": "seradotcom"
      },
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "body": "Pre-R16 maintainer preflight coordination (audit branch only; your worktree/branch is untouched):\n\n1. Exact current-main SHA 241000c268d1bf1dc29d4e91a913097ac0d020cb is not green: Windows ARM64 job 108839165329 in run 36394993424 fails real_win32_fixture_exercises_uia_without_pixel_fallback at exact UIA inspection with StaleReference after BLOCKED_NONINTERACTIVE_OCCLUSION. x64 and both sealed-tool compatibility jobs pass. Please reconcile the fixture lifecycle/root cause; the occlusion message alone does not explain away the later failed assertion. https://github.com/seradotcom/semwright/actions/runs/36394993424/job/108839165329\n\n2. In the reviewed run-interactive-certification.ps1 diff, Invoke-CargoRow and the secure_spawn_authority loop mark PASS from cargo exit code alone. A stale/misspelled test filter can select zero tests and still exit 0. Please require positive executed-test counts (and no ignored-only success), with a regression for a zero-selected run, before accepting PASS_WINDOWS_INTERACTIVE.\n\n3. The workflow diff currently uses runs-on: [self-hosted, Windows], although the PR description requires a dedicated semwright-interactive label. Please retain explicit disposable-runner targeting and operator approval; do not dispatch interactive tests to a generic connected Windows machine.\n\nI am correcting the review-bundle destructive-output behavior and reconciling root README/VERIFY/compatibility/changelog claims separately. R16 remains OPEN. No independent-review claim is being made.",
